#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1051 expect=violation domain=SQDM
#note "DISCRIMINATING. The corpus's first exercise of the SQ-- scope token. SQDM is 4 characters, so the SQ-- token (prefix 'SQ' + exactly two characters) matches it and the rule runs; RDOMAIN=DM with IDVAR populated fires the first disjunct. If this SKIPS, the prefix+2 reading of SQ-- is wrong -- escalate to stage R, do not edit this fixture."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 IDVAR=USUBJID
dataset SQDM label="Supplemental Qualifiers for DM"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 | USUBJID |  | RACEOTH | ASIAN-INDIAN
